{"author":{"id":"038d65070aa747b6bc9d50939fa697ec871a40ed259db54429b255bbef2581d6"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1792765468,"nonce":"K2u7uDHusMEdNQo/Bk9VkbcRM/E=","message":"Landed in 55df196edf755400c56373c015a78227767d0365.\n\nExtensions with native declarations, including built-in Git, now select a dedicated rayde-extension-host process. Script-only extensions remain embedded. Native approvals and hash validation still apply. The packaged host is resolved beside the program rather than through the workspace or PATH, and missing hosts do not fall back to embedded native execution. The host runs the existing VM and RayDE Markdown/syntax built-ins without an Ashui/GPU instance. Settings shows its PID, and its command line identifies the extension.\n\nThe parent uses asynchronous launch, pipe I/O and reaping, with 16 MiB framed-message limits, 32 MiB transport byte budgets, count limits and a 64 KiB stderr tail. Native output is validated before reaching the UI. The parent reserves its shutdown supervisor before launch; stop/disable/reload requests graceful shutdown and kills/reaps after one second if cleanup stalls. The child reserves a parent-loss watchdog before native code can run. Output and process exit wake the UI; no idle supervisor poll timer is added. Host failure releases pending replies, commands, owner registrations and presentations/tabs. Restarts create a fresh VM without replaying failed mutating commands. Native heap sizes remain extension-controlled; first-party built-ins and the editor bridge remain RayDE maintenance responsibilities.\n\nValidation:\n- 25 Rust checks passed, including actual host queue pressure, framing/schema rejection, asynchronous startup failure, process reaping and transport-owner release.\n- NativeExtensionChecks passed: separate process/native PIDs, script exception containment, Markdown/syntax services, view collection, native abort survival, deliberate 32 MiB native retention followed by a hung call, nonblocking Stop and verified process disappearance, malformed/oversized native stdout rejection, input size rejection, graceful shutdown and supervised restart without replaying a write.\n- NativeExtensionViewChecks passed: crash clears node models, roots and editor tab notifications.\n- ExtensionIdleWindow passed in process mode: delayed output wakes a quiet native window with no supervisor timer.\n- Full editor Checks passed against the final Haxe changes.\n- Git snapshots passed in both themes through the process host, including sidebar, expanded history, references, selection, scrolling, diff, cleanup, bulk-close reopening and fiber recovery. Dark expanded history and light SCM snapshots inspected.\n- Final parent-loss probe: native host phys_footprint 2,523,640 bytes before deliberate retention, 36,143,656 bytes after retaining 32 MiB. Idle CPU time stayed 0:00.01 across a two-second observation. After entering a native hang and losing parent stdin, it exited in 1.070 seconds. This is a minimal fixture host, not a Git or whole-editor memory baseline.\n- Rebuilt bin/rayde, bin/rayde.hl and the AOT RayDE.app; staged the bridge and packaged host, signed the nested executable and app, and passed strict deep signature verification. An isolated Git workspace app launch exited 0, used Contents/MacOS/rayde-extension-host --extension git with the packaged extension root, and left no native host after app exit.\n- git diff --check and shell syntax checks passed. Added scripts/check-native-extensions.sh for reproducible native lifecycle/window checks.","files":null}]}